 "title": "Welcome to Dodge County, MN",
 "text": "Welcome to Dodge County, MN\nSearch toggle\nDodge County, MN\nHome\nDepartments\n-Administration\nCounty Administrator\nEmployee Relations\nExtension\nFinance\nInformation Technology\n-Attorney\n-Court Administration\n-Court Services/Probation\n-Drug Court\n-Economic Development Authority\n-Emergency Management\n-Environmental Services\nGarbage/Recycling\nRenovation ReUse\nSeptic Systems\nWater Quality\nZoning\n-Extension\n-Fairview Care Center\n-Highway Department\nParks and Trails\n-Human Services (MNPrairie)\n-Land Records\nAssessor\nRecorder\nGIS & Maps\nSurveyor\n-Public Health\n-Sheriff\n-Soil & Water Conservation District\n-Veteran Services\n-Victim Services\n-Women's Shelter\nGovernment\nCounty Board\nDistrict 1\nDistrict 2\nDistrict 3\nDistrict 4\nDistrict 5\nBoard Agendas & Minutes\nI Want To\n-Apply for...\n-Connect to Social Media...\n-Contact...\nThe Midway Calendar\n-Find...\n-Live in Dodge County...\n-Pay or Purchase...\n-Play...\n-Request...\n-Report...\n-Volunteer...\n-View Photo Gallery\n-Learn about COVID-19...\n-Work\nContact Us\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nTRANSLATE\nAfrikaans\nAlbanian\nArabic\nArmenian\nAzerbaijani\nBasque\nBelarusian\nBengali\nBosnian\nBulgarian\nCatalan\nCebuano\nChinese (Simplified)\nChinese (Traditional)\nCroatian\nCzech\nDanish\nDutch\nEnglish\nEsperanto\nEstonian\nFilipino\nFinnish\nFrench\nGalician\nGeorgian\nGerman\nGreek\nGujarati\nHaitian Creole\nHausa\nHebrew\nHindi\nHmong\nHungarian\nIcelandic\nIgbo\nIndonesian\nIrish\nItalian\nJapanese\nJavanese\nKannada\nKhmer\nKorean\nLao\nLatin\nLatvian\nLithuanian\nMacedonian\nMalay\nMaltese\nMaori\nMarathi\nMongolian\nNepali\nNorwegian\nPersian\nPolish\nPortuguese\nPunjabi\nRomanian\nRussian\nSerbian\nSlovak\nSlovenian\nSomali\nSpanish\nSwahili\nSwedish\nTamil\nTelugu\nThai\nTurkish\nUkrainian\nUrdu\nVietnamese\nWelsh\nYiddish\nYoruba\nZulu\nGo\nPrev Next\nAssessor\nSub Menu\nLand Records\nAssessor\nValue and Classification Appeals\nAbatements and Disaster Credits\nAssessor's Duties\nHomesteads\nFrequently Asked Questions\nLinks\nImportant Dates\nTax Searches\nMobile Home Title Transfer\nRecorder\nBirth Certificates\nDeath Certificates\nDrivers Licenses\nMarriage Licenses\nOrdinations\nProperty Watch\nGIS/Maps\nSurveyor\nHome Land Records Assessor\nOur building hours are 8:00 am - 4:30 pm.\nThe County Assessor and staff are responsible for identifying, classifying, and valuing all real property and some classes of personal property within the boundaries of the County for ad valorum taxation purposes.\nEach assessment period begins on January 2nd of each year for computing the taxes which will be payable the following year. Appeals of the estimated market values and classifications are heard at the Local Board of Appeal and Equalization (LBAE) meetings or open book meetings for each local jurisdiction during the second half of April. Only appeals to the Local Boards are eligible to continuance to the County Board of Appeal and Equalization (CBAE) in June.\nHomestead Applications are accepted any time up to December 31st for taxes payable the following year. Quintile and new construction inspections are generally made between early summer and late winter for the new assessment year.\nCounty Assessor Office Information\nDirector of Land Records/County Assessor Ryan DeCook\nCounty Assessor Office Phone Number (507) 635-6245\nCounty Assessor Fax Number (507) 635-6265\nCounty Assessor Address 721 Main Street North\nMantorville, MN 55955\nCounty Assessor Email dodge.assessor@dodgecountymn.gov\nClick here to access Property Information\n© 2019 Dodge County, MN\n| Accessibility\n| Contact Us\nPowered by\n, The Government Website Experts |\nLogin\nSHARE\n×\nShare this page\nCopy and paste this code into your website.\n<a href=\"http://www.co.dodge.mn.us/departments/land_records/assessor.php\">Your Link Name</a>\nShare this page on your favorite Social network\nFacebook\nTwitter\nGoogle Plus\nReddit\nClose\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\